p window and result2 would remain in backoff (returncode!=0), failing the assert at :509 unmodified"],"finding":"The plan asserts the shared backoff state file's only test consumer is test_autodeploy_prune.py:86 and that 'no existing test reads that path' for the mcp failure backoff, but test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py:506 reads/unlinks state/deploy-backoff on the mcp failure->retry path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f821bacdd83abb2b0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan § 'Consumers outside autodeploy.sh' (\"The one test consumer of the shared STATE FILE is tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py:86\"; \"no existing test reads that path\")","norm_id":"n03e9dda775066e69","priority":1.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running tests/scripts/ after the mcp backoff is narrowed to mcp-deploy-backoff: the mcp unhealthy-retry test breaks because it clears the wrong file"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py:506 must be updated to unlink state/mcp-deploy-backoff (the mcp-narrowed file) instead of/in addition to state/deploy-backoff, and revise the plan sentence that claims prune.py:86 is the sole shared-state-file consumer and that no test reads the mcp backoff path.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the AUTODEPLOY_ERROR consumer inventory by grepping the token as a string across tests/, and add the omitted consumers — at minimum test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py (:490, :621) and test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py (:111), plus the observability coldstart/offsets fixtures — stating why each is or is not affected by the component=mcp reason change.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.515,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: \"Test consumers of the marker: test_autodeploy_review_drain.py, test_autodeploy_health_gate.py, test_observability_rotation_2dc7.py, test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py.\"","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py:490 `assert _markers(result, \"AUTODEPLOY_ERROR\")` and :621 `ln.startswith(\"AUTODEPLOY_ERROR \")` — asserts on the mcp failure path this ticket edits.","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py:111 `re.search(r\"^AUTODEPLOY_ERROR (\\{.*\\})$\", ...)`.","tests/scripts/test_observability_coldstart_e2a6.py:82 and test_observability_offsets_6a65.py:58 both feed `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` journal lines."],"finding":"The plan's enumeration of the AUTODEPLOY_ERROR marker's test consumers is incomplete. It lists exactly test_autodeploy_review_drain.py, test_autodeploy_health_gate.py, test_observability_rotation_2dc7.py, test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py, but a string sweep for AUTODEPLOY_ERROR shows further asserting consumers the plan omits — most notably test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py, which asserts the mcp failure path emits the marker (the very path